Collection of Algae...]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1783: Chloracidobacterium thermophilum Midnight Medium (CTM-Medium) (https://mediadive.dsmz.de/pdf/1783)\nciteturn11view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 4; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://mediadive.dsmz.de/pdf/1783\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 119\nL0@P0: 1783: Chloracidobacterium thermophilum Midnight Medium (CTM-M\nL1@P0: Final pH: 7.0\nL2@P0: Final volume: 1000 ml\nL3@P0: 1. The CTM-Medium consists of two parts. Part one is autoclavable and called CTM-Medium\nL4@P0: basis. Part two is named mixed solution and contains non-autoclavable components. Solid\nL5@P0: CTM-Medium contains 1% three times washed Bactoagar and is added to the CTM-Medium\nL6@P0: basis prior autoclaving.\nL7@P0: 2. Note: Bacto peptone can be omitted with only using amino acids as carbon source,\nL8@P0: which will maker it a defined medium. Amount of amino acids will then have to be\nL9@P0: increased to 100mg/L each.\nL10@P0: Solution 1 20.000 ml\nL11@P0: Solution 2 3.000 ml\nL12@P0: Solution 3 2.000 ml\nL13@P0: Solution 4 2.500 ml\nL14@P0: HEPES buffer 2.400 g\nL15@P0: 3. Make up to 970 ml with distilled water.\nL16@P0: 4. Adjust pH to 7.0 with NaOH (2M).\nL17@P0: 5. Autoclave at 121 °C for 20 min.\nL18@P0: 6. Seal medium bottle immediately after autoclaving in order to avoid oxygenation.\nL19@P0: 7. Cool down to 70 °C (in a water bath).\nL20@P0: 8. Add mixed solution to the CTM basis for completing the CTM-Medium (30 mL),\nL21@P0: 9. Note: Always prepare freshly! Mix the following components (e.g., in a volume of\nL22@P0: approx. 30 mL) and add the filter sterilized mixture to the autoclaved CTM-Medium basis:\nL23@P0: NaHCO3 (or 10 mL of a 6.25% solution in water) 0.625 g\nL24@P0: Na-thioglycolate (or use 1 mL of a 12.5% solution in water, autoclaved under a N2\nL25@P0: gasphase) 0.125 g\nL26@P0: Solution 5 0.500 ml\nL27@P0: Solution 6 20.000 ml\nL28@P0: Vitamin solution A (1000 x stock) 0.250 ml\nL29@P0: Vitamin solution B (1000 x stock) 0.250 ml\nL30@P0: 10. Keep CTM-Medium tightly sealed and between 50-70˚C prior usage.\nL31@P0: 11. It is strongly recommended to use up the CTM-Medium as soon as possible after\nL32@P0: preparation! Short term storage of CTM-Medium basis possible under strictly anaerobic\nL33@P0: conditions. Mixed solutions should then be added freshly before use.\nL34@P0: 12. Pour CTM-Medium into flasks, bottles or similar and leave a quarter air headspace and\nL35@P0: seal them.\nL36@P0-1: © 2026 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 1 of 41783: Chloracidobacterium thermophilum Midnight Medium (CTM-Medium)\nL37@P1: Solution 1\nL38@P1: 1. This is a 50x stock stock solution.\nL39@P1: MgSO4 x 7 H2O 3.75 g\nL40@P1: CaCl2 x 2 H2O 1.80 g\nL41@P1: Citric acid 0.30 g\nL42@P1: Na-EDTA x 2 H2O (pH 8, 0,25 M) 0.60 ml\nL43@P1: Trace metal solution 50.00 ml\nL44@P1: 2. Make up to 1000 ml with distilled water.\nL45@P1: 3. Autoclave at 121 °C for 20 min.\nL46@P1: Trace metal solution\nL47@P1: H3BO3 2.860 g\nL48@P1: MnCl2 x 4 H2O 1.810 g\nL49@P1: ZnSO4 x 7 H2O 0.222 g\nL50@P1: Na2MoO4 x 2 H2O 0.390 g\nL51@P1: CuSO4 x 5 H2O 0.079 g\nL52@P1: Co(NO3)2 x 6 H2O 0.049 g\nL53@P1: Distilled water 1000.000 ml\nL54@P1: Solution 2\nL55@P1: K2HPO4 15.30\nL56@P1: 1. Make up to 1000 ml with distilled water.\nL57@P1: 2. Autoclave at 121 °C for 20 min.\nL58@P1: Solution 3\nL59@P1: Ferric ammonium citrate 12.00 g\nL60@P1: 1. Make up to 1000 ml with distilled water.\nL61@P1: 2. Autoclave at 121 °C for 20 min.\nL62@P1: Solution 4\nL63@P1: 2-Oxoglutarate 14.60 g\nL64@P1: 1. Make up to 1000 ml with distilled water.\nL65@P1: 2. Autoclave at 121 °C for 20 min.\nL66@P1-2: © 2026 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 2 of 41783: Chloracidobacterium thermophilum Midnight Medium (CTM-Medium)\nL67@P2: Vitamin solution A (1000 x stock) (from medium 1783)\nL68@P2: Biotin 10.00 mg\nL69@P2: Riboflavin 10.00 mg\nL70@P2: Thiamine HCl 100.00 mg\nL71@P2: Thiamine pyrophosphate 100.00 mg\nL72@P2: L-Ascorbic acid 100.00 mg\nL73@P2: Calcium pantothenate 100.00 mg\nL74@P2: Folic acid 100.00 mg\nL75@P2: Nicotinamide 100.00 mg\nL76@P2: Nicotinic acid 100.00 mg\nL77@P2: p-Aminobenzoic acid 100.00 mg\nL78@P2: Pyridoxine hydrochloride 100.00 mg\nL79@P2: Lipoic acid 100.00 mg\nL80@P2: beta-NAD 100.00 mg\nL81@P2: Potassium phosphate buffer (pH 7.2, 10 mM) 100.00 ml\nL82@P2: 1. Dissolve the vitamins in 10mM phosphate buffer, pH7.2.\nL83@P2: 2. Titrate with NaOH until vitamins are dissolved, filter sterilize afterwards, and freeze in\nL84@P2: appropriate aliquots until usage.\nL85@P2: Vitamin solution B (1000 x stock) (from medium 1783)\nL86@P2: Vitamin B12 100.00 mg\nL87@P2: Distilled water 100.00 ml\nL88@P2: 1. Dissolve the vitamin B12 in water.\nL89@P2: 2. Titrate with HCl until vitamin B12 is dissolved, filter sterilize afterwards, and freeze in\nL90@P2: appropriate aliquots until usage.\nL91@P2: Solution 5\nL92@P2: Bacto peptone (BD-Difco) 10.00 g\nL93@P2: Distilled water 100.00 ml\nL94@P2: Autoclave at 121 °C for 20 min.\nL95@P2: Solution 6\nL96@P2: L-Alanine 100.00 mg\nL97@P2: L-Arginine 100.00 mg\nL98@P2: L-Asparagine 100.00 mg\nL99@P2: L-Aspartic acid 100.00 mg\nL100@P2: L-Cysteine 100.00 mg\nL101@P2: L-Glutamic acid 100.00 mg\nL102@P2-3: © 2026 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 3 of 41783: Chloracidobacterium thermophilum Midnight Medium (CTM-Medium)\nL103@P3: L-Glutamine 100.00 mg\nL104@P3: Glycine 100.00 mg\nL105@P3: L-Histidine 100.00 mg\nL106@P3: L-Isoleucine 100.00 mg\nL107@P3: L-Leucine 100.00 mg\nL108@P3: L-Lysine 100.00 mg\nL109@P3: L-Methionine 100.00 mg\nL110@P3: L-Phenylalanine 100.00 mg\nL111@P3: L-Proline 100.00 mg\nL112@P3: L-Serine 100.00 mg\nL113@P3: L-Threonine 100.00 mg\nL114@P3: L-Tryptophan 100.00 mg\nL115@P3: L-Tyrosine 100.00 mg\nL116@P3: L-Valine 100.00 mg\nL117@P3: Distilled water 400.00 ml\nL118@P3: © 2026 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 4 of 4\n"
